From: Alejandro Exojo Piqueras <suy@badopi.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Add CSI u support for Ctrl+Backspace word deletion

PasteAwareTextInput already has word deletion logic (deletePreviousWord),
but it only triggers on legacy sequences: ESC+DEL (Alt+Backspace), ESC+BS,
and Ctrl+W (\x17).

Terminals using the CSI u encoding (Kitty keyboard protocol) send
"\x1B[127;5u" for Ctrl+Backspace (DEL code + Ctrl modifier), or
"\x1B[8;5u" (BS code + Ctrl modifier). These sequences are not matched,
so Ctrl+Backspace falls through to the TextInput child component, which
ignores the Ctrl modifier and deletes a single character.

Add the CSI u sequences to the raw input handler so Ctrl+Backspace
triggers deletePreviousWord(), matching the behavior of Ctrl+W and
Alt+Backspace.

This was tested with Konsole (custom keytab sending "\E[127;5u") through
tmux with `extended-keys always`.

--- a/src/cli/components/PasteAwareTextInput.tsx
+++ b/src/cli/components/PasteAwareTextInput.tsx
@@ -xxx,xxx +xxx,xxx @@
       // Forward delete: handled by parent's raw input handler
       if (sequence === "\x1B[3~" || /^\x1b\[3;\d+~$/.test(sequence)) {
         ...
       }
+      // CSI u format for Ctrl+Backspace (e.g. from Konsole keytab)
+      if (sequence === "\x1B[127;5u" || sequence === "\x1B[8;5u") {
+        deletePreviousWord();
+        return;
+      }
       // Alt+Backspace (ESC+DEL), Alt+Backspace variant (ESC+BS), Ctrl+W
       if (sequence === "\x1B\x7f" || sequence === "\x1B\b" || sequence === "\x17") {
         deletePreviousWord();
         return;
       }
